    "reply": "EGFR mutations in non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) are well-documented in ClinVar with 25 distinct variants in the EGFR gene (NM_005228.5), and at least five clinical trials are evaluating EGFR-targeted therapies for NSCLC patients [6][1].\n\n## EGFR Sequence Variants\n\nThe ClinVar registry contains numerous EGFR missense and synonymous variants catalogued under transcript NM_005228.5, including p.Asn280Lys (ClinVar:1000076), p.Arg222Cys (ClinVar:1000203), p.Arg165Gln (ClinVar:1000496), p.Gln218Lys (ClinVar:1000546), and p.Thr605Ala (ClinVar:1000851) [6][7][8][9][10]. Additional variants include p.Ser885Ala (ClinVar:1000960), p.Gly331Arg (ClinVar:1001152), p.Trp608Arg (ClinVar:1001187), p.Pro520Leu (ClinVar:1001705), and p.Pro914Arg (ClinVar:1001710) [11][12][13][14][15]. A synonymous variant, p.Gly873= (ClinVar:1001782), is also recorded alongside missense changes such as p.Ile780Thr (ClinVar:1002380), p.Gln557Arg (ClinVar:1002493), p.Thr241Ala (ClinVar:1002562), and p.Val1011Leu (ClinVar:1002578) [16][17][18][19][20]. Further variants include p.Ser1070Asn (ClinVar:1002794), p.Thr488Ser (ClinVar:1003132), p.Arg973Gly (ClinVar:1003262), p.Ser350Cys (ClinVar:1003305), and p.His559Tyr (ClinVar:1003743) [21][22][23][24][25]. Rounding out the set are p.Val659Leu (ClinVar:1003794), p.Met945Val (ClinVar:1004032), p.Gln181Glu (ClinVar:1004363), p.Ile580Thr (ClinVar:1004409), and p.Asn528Asp (ClinVar:1004521) [26][27][28][29][30].\n\n## EGFR-TKI Clinical Trials\n\nA retrospective study comparing gefitinib, erlotinib, and osimertinib in NSCLC patients is registered, as is a survival-outcome study of EGFR-TKIs in uncommon EGFR-mutant advanced NSCLC [1][2]. A trial of osimertinib for advanced EGFR-positive NSCLC patients is also listed [3].\n\n## Special-Setting and Cellular Therapy Trials\n\nA CSF analysis trial is enrolling EGFR-mutant NSCLC patients with leptomeningeal disease, and an EGFR/B7H3 CAR-T cell therapy trial targeting lung cancer and triple-negative breast cancer is registered [4][5].",
